  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTING SUMATRAN ELEPHANT POPULATIONS AND HABITAT THROUGH ELEPHANT RESPONSE UNITS (ERU) IN COLLABORATION WITH LOCAL COMMUNITIES IN WAY KAMBAS NATIONAL PARK, LAMPUNG PROVINCE, INDONESIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO PROTECT THE INTEGRITY OF WAY KAMBAS NATIONAL PARK (WKNP) AND ITS CRITICALLY ENDANGERED POPULATION OF SUMATRAN ELEPHANTS AND TO PROMOTE HUMAN ELEPHANT COEXISTENCE WITH LOCAL COMMUNITIES. THROUGH THE DEPLOYMENT OF ELEPHANT RESPONSE UNITS (ERU) AND IN CLOSE COLLABORATION WITH WKNP AUTHORITIES AND FOREST POLICE, THIS PROJECT WILL MONITOR, MITIGATE, AND PREVENT HUMAN ELEPHANT CONFLICT (HEC), EMPOWER LOCAL COMMUNITIES, PROVIDE CARE FOR AND MANAGEMENT OF ERU ELEPHANTS, AND DETECT AND PREVENT ILLEGAL ACTIVITIES IN AND AROUND THE PARK. ERUS EMPLOY ELEPHANTS AND THEIR SKILLED HANDLERS ALONG WITH TRAINED LOCAL COMMUNITY MEMBERS TO CONDUCT REGULAR FOREST PATROLS TO DETECT AND PREVENT ILLEGAL ACTIVITIES, MONITOR WILD ASIAN ELEPHANT HERDS, AND MITIGATE CONFLICT BETWEEN ELEPHANTS AND LOCAL COMMUNITIES. PROJECT ACTIVITIES INCLUDE (1) EQUIPPING (FIRE EXTINGUISHERS, CAMERAS, LAPTOP AND PRINTERS, BOOTS, RAINCOATS, BACKPACKS, GPS UNITS, HEADLAMPS, RADIOS, UNIFORMS, BACKPACK SPRAYERS, MOSQUITO REPELLENT, FIRST AID SUPPLIES, RATIONS, ELEPHANT FOOD AND VITAMINS, HOSES, SACKS, AND OFFICE MATERIALS) AND OPERATING 4 ERU TEAMS AND CAMPS, TOTALING 65 STAFF AND 27 ELEPHANTS (2) ERU HABITAT PATROLS AND WILD ELEPHANT MONITORING (3) MAINTAINING GPS COLLARS ON SIX WILD ELEPHANTS, COLLECTING AND ANALYZING RESULT</narrative>
  </description>
